{"name":"Garland","hex":"#69887b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Garland","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname originating as an occupation for a maker or seller of garlands.","A male given name transferred from the surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Garland"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garland","blocks":[{"text":"A garland is a decorative braid, knot or wreath of flowers, leaves, or other material. Garlands can be worn on the head or around the neck, hung on an inanimate object, or laid in a place of cultural or religious importance. In contemporary times, garlands are used to decorate, especially around holidays."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Choinka.JPG/330px-Choinka.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garland","wikidata":"Q756600"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Daisy_chain.JPG/500px-Daisy_chain.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Daisy_chain.JPG/1280px-Daisy_chain.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Daisy_chain.JPG/500px-Daisy_chain.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A daisy chain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADaisy_chain.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Richard_Redgrave_%281804-1888%29_-_Ophelia_Weaving_Her_Garlands_%28from_William_Shakespeare%27s_%27Hamlet%27%29_-_FA.171%28O%29_-_Victoria_and_Albert_Museum.jpg/500px-Richard_Redgrave_%281804-1888%29_-_Ophelia_Weaving_Her_Garlands_%28from_William_Shakespeare%27s_%27Hamlet%27%29_-_FA.171%28O%29_-_Victoria_and_Albert_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con